WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-compute (90s) Narrator Nylo

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.833
First, every calculation is a physical event where flipping silicon switches spends real energy in joules.

2
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:15.990
Second, honest hardware audits separate wire current sensors from chip counters, while sleeping between real jobs.

3
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:25.077
Third, single-cycle Boolean lookup circuits replace heavy decimal arithmetic on repeated checks with tiny hardware steps.

4
00:00:25.577 --> 00:00:31.125
Built-in processor energy counters work like a dashboard fuel estimate—helpful over long

5
00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:37.051
trips, yet blind to sub-millisecond bursts and shared background noise. Physical current-shunt

6
00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:42.473
sensors sit directly on the circuit-board power rail and measure real electrical draw.

7
00:00:42.973 --> 00:00:49.368
On compute dot openie dot dev, we organize two hundred fifty-eight primitives across

8
00:00:49.368 --> 00:00:56.600
thirty-three families. First, halt idle clocks until real work arrives; second, compile dynamic

9
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:03.755
code into tight binaries; third, run frozen decisions in single-cycle Boolean lookup circuits.

10
00:01:04.255 --> 00:01:10.532
Compiling interpreted validation loops into native machine code cut measured energy twentyfold. On

11
00:01:10.532 --> 00:01:16.745
edge modules equipped with inline power-rail current shunts, compiled execution drew nine hundred

12
00:01:16.745 --> 00:01:23.021
twenty-seven point three microjoules while paged lookup arrays ran at two hundred fifty megahertz.

13
00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:28.633
Whether an energy reading comes from a physical wire shunt, a processor counter,

14
00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:33.681
or a circuit simulation, stating its exact instrument keeps engineering honest.
